import lib/process.dl

to get [the|] process kill test interpreter:
    return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set command to a process command for the process kill test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import time;time.sleep(10)" as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it
print line child was launched
kill child and set killed to it
print line killed succeeded
wait up to 2000 milliseconds for child and set finished to it
print lines ((finished succeeded) and (finished reports completion)) and (finished reports termination)
kill child and set repeated to it
print line repeated succeeded
clean up child and set cleaned to it
print line cleaned succeeded
